ion","volume":"69","year":"2021","journal-title":"Current opinion in structural biology"},{"key":"2022090512450616000_2022.09.01.506224v1.24","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/j.jmb.2008.04.024"},{"key":"2022090512450616000_2022.09.01.506224v1.25","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1073\/pnas.96.17.9716"},{"key":"2022090512450616000_2022.09.01.506224v1.26","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1038\/nature05385"},{"key":"2022090512450616000_2022.09.01.506224v1.27","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"msab321","DOI":"10.1093\/molbev\/msab321","article-title":"Modeling sequence-space exploration and emergence of epistatic signals in protein evolution","volume":"39","year":"2022","journal-title":"Molecular biology and evolution"},{"key":"2022090512450616000_2022.09.01.506224v1.28","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/j.cub.2014.09.072"},{"key":"2022090512450616000_2022.09.01.506224v1.29","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.7554\/eLife.16965"},{"key":"2022090512450616000_2022.09.01.506224v1.30","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1126\/science.1123539"},{"key":"2022090512450616000_2022.09.01.506224v1.31","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"691","DOI":"10.1038\/s41587-020-00793-4","article-title":"Deep diversification of an AAV capsid protein by machine learning","volume":"39","year":"2021","journal-title":"Nature Biotechnology"},{"key":"2022090512450616000_2022.09.01.506224v1.32","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1007\/BF00623322"},{"key":"2022090512450616000_2022.09.01.506224v1.33","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1038\/nature09929"},{"key":"2022090512450616000_2022.09.01.506224v1.34","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"1946","DOI":"10.1016\/j.cell.2018.10.021","article-title":"Scalable, continuous evolution of genes at mutation rates above genomic error thresholds","volume":"175","year":"2018","journal-title":"Cell"},{"key":"2022090512450616000_2022.09.01.506224v1.35","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"248","DOI":"10.1038\/s41586-018-0384-8","article-title":"CRISPR-guided DNA polymerases enable diversification of all nucleotides in a tunable window","volume":"560","year":"2018","journal-title":"Nature"},{"key":"2022090512450616000_2022.09.01.506224v1.36","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1073\/pnas.1422285112"},{"key":"2022090512450616000_2022.09.01.506224v1.37","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1371\/journal.pone.0006441"},{"key":"2022090512450616000_2022.09.01.506224v1.38","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1093\/bioinformatics\/btr507"},{"key":"2022090512450616000_2022.09.01.506224v1.39","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"357","DOI":"10.1038\/nmeth.1923","article-title":"Fast gapped-read alignment with Bowtie 2","volume":"9","year":"2012","journal-title":"Nature methods"},{"key":"2022090512450616000_2022.09.01.506224v1.40","unstructured":"Paszke, A. et al. PyTorch: An Imperative Style, High-Performance Deep Learning Library in Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems 32 (eds Wallach, H. et al.) 8024\u20138035 (Curran Associates, Inc., 2019)."},{"key":"2022090512450616000_2022.09.01.506224v1.41","unstructured":"Stratagene, Agilent Technologies. GeneMorph II Random Mutagenesis Kit version Revision A.01. Agilent Technologies (Agilent Technologies, Inc. 2009, 2009)."},{"key":"2022090512450616000_2022.09.01.506224v1.42","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"304","DOI":"10.2144\/97232rr01","article-title":"Generation of large libraries of random mutants in Bacillus subtilis by PCR-based plasmid multimerization","volume":"23","year":"1997","journal-title":"Biotechniques"}],"link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/syndication.highwire.org\/content\/doi\/10.1101\/2022.09.01.506224","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2026,1,15]],"date-time":"2026-01-15T03:33:24Z","timestamp":1768448004000},"score":36.605423,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"http:\/\/biorxiv.org\/lookup\/doi\/10.1101\/2022.09.01.506224"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2022,9,2]]},"references-count":42,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1101\/2022.09.01.506224","relation":{"is-preprint-of":[{"id-type":"doi","id":"10.1371\/journal.pcbi.1010956","asserted-by":"subject"}]},"published":{"date-parts":[[2022,9,2]]},"subtype":"preprint"},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,15]],"date-time":"2026-10-15T00:44:21Z","timestamp":1792025061089,"version":"4.4.0"},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"Bentham Science Publishers Ltd.","issue":"1","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["TOVJ"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2009,4,2]]},"DOI":"10.2174\/1874357900903010001","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2009,4,2]],"date-time":"2009-04-02T17:17:58Z","timestamp":1238692678000},"page":"1-6","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":126,"title":["The Evolution of Viruses in Multi-Host Fitness Landscapes"],"prefix":"10.2174","volume":"3","author":[{"given":"Santiago F.","family":"Elena","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Patricia","family":"Agudelo-Romero","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Jasna","family":"Lalic","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"965","container-title":["The Open Virology Journal"],"language":"en","deposited":{"date-parts":[[2015,2,17]],"date-time":"2015-02-17T19:06:16Z","timestamp":1424199976000},"score":32.683983,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"http:\/\/benthamopen.com\/ABSTRACT\/TOVJ-3-1"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2009,4,2]]},"references-count":0,"journal-issue":{"issue":"1","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2009,4,2]]}},"alternative-id":["LiveAll1"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.2174\/1874357900903010001","ISSN":["1874-3579"],"issn-type":[{"value":"1874-3579","type":"print"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[2009,4,2]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,9,22]],"date-time":"2026-09-22T13:10:33Z","timestamp":1790082633076,"version":"4.0.1"},"publisher":"Human Frontier Science Program","award":"LT00169\/2008-L","DOI":"10.52044\/hfsp.lt001692008-l.pc.gr.166332","type":"grant","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,4]],"date-time":"2026-03-04T07:54:17Z","timestamp":1772610857000},"source":"Crossref","prefix":"10.52044","member":"14406","project":[{"project-title":[{"title":"Exploring wiring principles of protein-protein interaction networks by directed in vivo evolution","language":"en"}],"project-description":[{"description":"In living cells almost all transfers of mass (e.g. chemical reactions), information or energy involve protein-protein interactions (PPIs). For this reason, understanding PPIs is key to comprehending all biological processes. Despite the importance of PPIs, the mechanisms by which they are created during the course of evolution are still poorly understood. An estimated 1,600 to 16,000 PPIs have been re-wired between human and chimpanzee. This high turnover of PPIs implies a high evolvability, i.e., that the number of mutations needed to create a new PPI is low. I would like to investigate this issue and quantify in molecular terms how easy it is to create a new PPI. To this end I will use in vivo directed evolution to engineer new PPIs, and dissect and rationalize the sets of mutations found to trigger new interactions. This will allow me to estimate several parameters that describe the evolvability of PPIs, and determine how these parameters depend on certain factors such as protein family, sequence similarity to a known binder, or functional constraints. This project will provide an estimate of the basal \u201cstickiness\u201d (i.e., the intrinsic propensity to interact weakly and non-specifically) of proteins for each other, and the rate at which the strength and specificity of this basal stickiness can be improved by introducing mutations. This knowledge is fundamental to a better understanding of the principles of formation and evolution of PPIs, and for finding and designing drugs that modulate them. In addition, this project will provide a novel strategy to engineer PPIs in vivo, which has implications to protein design as well as nanotechnology.","language":"en"}],"lead-investigator":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-8959-7365","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Emmanuel","family":"LEVY","affiliation":[{"id":[{"id":"https:\/\/ror.org\/01swzsf04","id-type":"ROR","asserted-by":"publisher"}],"name":"University of Geneva (Universit\u00e9 de Gen\u00e8ve)"}]}],"award-amount":{"amount":0.0,"currency":null},"award-start":{"date-parts":[[2009,1,1]]},"funding":[{"type":"award","funder":{"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/100004412","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}],"name":"Human Frontier Science Program"}}]}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2026,9,22]],"date-time":"2026-09-22T12:22:03Z","timestamp":1790079723000},"score":32.589245,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/proposalcentral.com\/Insights\/Crossref\/PublicAwardRedirect\/HFSP.LT001692008-L.pc.gr.166332"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2009,1,1]]},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.52044\/hfsp.lt001692008-l.pc.gr.166332"}],"items-per-page":5,"query":{"start-index":0,"search-terms":null}}}